{"name":"Fiorito","hex":"#bfbfaf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Fiorito","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Italian."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Fiorito"}],"entries":[{"title":"Villa Fiorito","blocks":[{"text":"Villa Fiorito is a city in the Lomas de Zamora Partido of Buenos Aires Province, to the south of central Buenos Aires, Argentina. It forms part of the Greater Buenos Aires urban conurbation. Many Italian and Spanish descendants live there. In recent decades people from other provinces have come to live near central Buenos Aires, creating new slums in the city. Diego Maradona, considered one of the best footballers of all time, was raised in Villa Fiorito."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Camino_de_la_Ribera_Sur_en_Villa_Fiorito.jpg/330px-Camino_de_la_Ribera_Sur_en_Villa_Fiorito.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Villa_Fiorito","wikidata":"Q2527509"},{"title":"Alfredo Fiorito","blocks":[{"text":"Alfredo Fiorito was an Argentine disc jockey. He has been credited as the \"Father of the Balearic beat\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfredo_Fiorito","wikidata":"Q4723775"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Sotto un albero fiorito - btv1b52512972j (8 of 8)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Sotto_un_albero_fiorito_-_btv1b52512972j_%288_of_8%29.jpg/500px-Sotto_un_albero_fiorito_-_btv1b52512972j_%288_of_8%29.jpg","ratio":1.2915766738660908,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sotto_un_albero_fiorito_-_btv1b52512972j_(8_of_8).jpg","share":0.296875},{"title":"Sotto un albero fiorito - btv1b52512972j (2 of 8)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Sotto_un_albero_fiorito_-_btv1b52512972j_%282_of_8%29.jpg/500px-Sotto_un_albero_fiorito_-_btv1b52512972j_%282_of_8%29.jpg","ratio":1.296476964